NAME
    gfx - the C graphics library (//#use gfx)

SYNOPSIS
    //#use gfx          at the top of a C program (cc splices /lib/lib_gfx.c)

DESCRIPTION
    A thin C veneer over the display device's registers ($FF20-$FF2F), so a
    program draws with calls instead of raw peek/poke. The device does the
    drawing itself, so a filled box costs the same as an empty one, and the
    same program behaves identically on the emulator and the board.

    The screen is 480x272 in RGB565 direct colour: a pixel IS its colour,
    r and b are 0-31, g is 0-63, 0 is black. Off-screen pixels are simply
    not drawn -- but the device treats coordinates as UNSIGNED, so a
    negative value lands far off the right/bottom, not off the left edge.

FUNCTIONS
    gpresent()            1 if a display is fitted -- CALL THIS FIRST: an
                          absent display floats the bus and every other
                          call would poke the void
    grgb(r,g,b)           pack a colour (fields masked)
    gcolor(c)             set the pen to a packed colour
    gcls()                clear the whole screen TO THE PEN colour
    gpixelw(x,y)          one pixel (was gplot)
    gline(x0,y0,x1,y1)    line, both endpoints drawn
    gbox(x0,y0,x1,y1)     rectangle outline (any two opposite corners)
    gboxf(...)            ... filled
    gcircle(x,y,r)        circle outline; gcirclef(...) filled
    gellipse(x,y,rx,ry)   ellipse outline; gellipsef(...) filled
                          (a circle IS the ellipse with rx=ry since the
                          stage-10 diet retired the separate circle
                          rasterizer -- same call, radius capped at 255,
                          r=0 draws nothing; gcls and gbox likewise ride
                          BOXFILL and four lines, same pixels)
    gpixelr(x,y)          the colour at (x,y); 0 off-screen
                          (was gpoint -- the pixel pair renamed
                          so POINT names only the PGC verb)
    gwait()               spin until the engine is idle (each call above
                          already waits before issuing, so back-to-back
                          calls are safe without it)

EXAMPLE
    //#use gfx
    int main() {
        if (gpresent() == 0) { puts("?No display"); return 1; }
        gcolor(0); gcls();
        gcolor(grgb(31, 0, 0));
        gboxf(40, 40, 200, 200);
        if (gpixelr(100, 100) == grgb(31, 0, 0)) { puts("RED"); }
        return 0;
    }

DRAWING MODES (stage 10f)
    The device register GMODE ($FF2E write side) sets the pixel-write
    mode for lines, points and outlines: 0 replace, 1 complement,
    2 OR, 3 AND, 4 XOR. Fills and gcls() always replace. There is no
    C wrapper yet -- poke(0xFF2E, m), or issue GL "LINFUN m" (man gl);
    the mode applies to this library's lines and outlines too.

NOTES
    The source is /lib/lib_gfx.c on this disk (and os/commands/lib_gfx.c in
    the repo); hand-asm programs get the same addresses as equates from
    /lib/gfx.inc via `;#use gfx`. BASIC reaches the same device through its
    own statements -- see man basic, GRAPHICS.

